  - spanish-dialects
abstract: >-
  Idiolect-G2P is a formal computational framework for inverse phonological
  disambiguation in Spanish texts. Unlike traditional feedforward G2P systems
  that assume a monolithic prescriptive standard, Idiolect-G2P utilizes rhyme
  constraints, post-lexical sandhi dynamics, and Clements & Hume feature geometry
  within a Maximum Entropy / Bayesian framework to retrospectively infer the
  author's underlying dialectal variety and continuous isogloss vector theta in [0, 1]^14.
